    a: "Most institutional deals run as a broker-led auction. The broker markets the property with an offering memorandum (OM) and a data room, takes first-round bids, then asks a shortlist for best-and-final offers. The winner agrees business terms in a letter of intent (LOI), signs a binding purchase and sale agreement (PSA) and posts a deposit. During due diligence the buyer inspects everything and can usually still walk away. Then the deposit goes hard and closing follows. The buyer's investment committee (IC) approves each stage.",
