    q: "Walk me through the acquisitions process, from sourcing a deal to closing.",
    a: "Source the deal, on or off market, and screen it. Sign a confidentiality agreement, get the OM and data room, underwrite and tour. Get IC approval to bid, then submit a first-round bid and, if shortlisted, a best-and-final. Once selected, negotiate the LOI and PSA and post a deposit. Run due diligence, usually 30–45 days, while arranging the loan. Take the deal back to IC before the deposit goes hard, then close a few weeks later.",
