    classic: true,
    q: "What are the key terms in a letter of intent, and is it binding?",
    a: "An LOI sets the business terms: price, deposit size and when it goes hard, the length of due diligence, the closing date, financing, any loan assumption and who pays which closing costs. It's mostly non-binding, so either side can still walk away, but provisions like exclusivity and confidentiality are usually written to bind.",
